  <!-- Deep Dive 1: LLVM SSA Compiler -->
  <section id="llvm-ssa" class="section-block">
    <span id="llvm" class="anchor-alias"></span>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="deep-dive-card card glass-card animate-fade-up">
        <div class="deep-dive-header">
          <div class="header-meta">
            <span class="badge badge-red">Ahead-of-Time Native Compilation</span>
            <span class="badge">Chunk 28</span>
            <span class="badge font-mono">src/llvm.rs &bull; lib/compiler/llvm.shae</span>
          </div>
          <h2>LLVM 18 SSA Compiler (<code>shae llvm</code>)</h2>
          <p class="deep-dive-lead">
            Shae implements direct code generation targeting compliant LLVM 18 Single Static Assignment (SSA) intermediate representation without requiring bulky C library wrapper dependencies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-dive-grid">
          <div class="deep-dive-text">
            <h3>Entry Block Alloca &amp; Register Promotion</h3>
            <p>
              Rather than generating complex &phi; (phi) nodes directly during AST traversal, Shae's LLVM frontend emits local variables into the function's <code>%entry</code> basic block using typed <code>alloca</code> instructions. LLVM's canonical <code>mem2reg</code> optimization pass automatically lifts these stack variables into hardware SSA virtual registers, ensuring maximum optimization without frontend bloat.
            </p>
            <h3>External C ABI Interoperability</h3>
            <p>
              The LLVM backend declares standard C ABI runtime symbols (<code>printf</code>, <code>puts</code>, <code>malloc</code>, <code>free</code>, <code>exit</code>), maps Shae functions to native calling conventions, and generates a standard <code>@main</code> entry point that initializes globals and runs top-level statements.
            </p>
            <h3>Clang -O2 Pipeline Integration</h3>
            <p>
              Using the <code>-c</code> flag, Shae automatically invokes the system Clang compiler with <code>-O2</code> optimization, producing standalone, stripped native executables ready for deployment.
            </p>

