            <span class="badge font-mono">src/buffer.rs &bull; examples/buffer_demo.shae</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Zero-Copy Typed Memory Buffers (<code>std:buffer</code>)</h2>
          <p class="deep-dive-lead">
            Engineered for high-volume network packet parsing, file formats, and IPC. A thread-safe container sharing underlying storage without heap copies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-dive-grid">
          <div class="deep-dive-text">
            <h3>Shared Arc Storage &amp; Zero-Allocation Slices</h3>
            <p>
              The <code>ByteBuffer</code> struct wraps <code>storage: Arc&lt;RwLock&lt;Vec&lt;u8&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> with local <code>offset</code> and <code>length</code> tracking. Calling <code>buf.slice(start, end)</code> creates a lightweight window pointing to the exact same storage without copying bytes. Mutating a byte in the child slice updates the parent buffer immediately.
            </p>
            <h3>Endian-Aware Multi-Byte Reads &amp; Writes</h3>
            <p>
              Read and write 16-bit, 32-bit, and 64-bit integers and floating-point values with explicit byte order:
              <code>read_u16_le</code>, <code>write_u16_be</code>, <code>read_u32_le</code>, <code>write_i64_be</code>, <code>read_f64_be</code>.
            </p>
            <h3>High-Performance Struct Packing Engine</h3>
            <p>
              Python-compatible format strings (e.g., <code>&lt;I2h4s</code> for Little-Endian u32, two i16s, and a 4-byte ASCII string) provide single-step packing and unpacking via <code>pack</code>, <code>unpack</code>, <code>pack_into</code>, and <code>calcsize</code>.
            </p>

