          <h2>TLS/mTLS Cluster Mesh &amp; Hot-Code Reloading (<code>std:actor:cluster</code>)</h2>
          <p class="deep-dive-lead">
            Zero-downtime actor logic swapping, schema migrations, and mutual TLS encryption across distributed clusters.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-dive-grid">
          <div class="deep-dive-text">
            <h3>Zero-Downtime Hot-Code Reloading</h3>
            <p>
              In production services, stopping an actor drops active state and pending mailbox requests. Shae introduces <code>ActorMessage::Reload</code>: an actor handler function is swapped atomically in place. The actor thread continues executing without dropping queued FIFO messages.
            </p>
            <h3>Live State Schema Migrations</h3>
            <p>
              When new code requires a different state schema, pass an optional migration closure: <code>actor.reload(new_handler, migration_fn)</code>. The migration function transforms the active state (e.g., from V2 plain map to V3 versioned schema) before the new handler processes the next message.
            </p>
            <h3>Distributed Cluster Mesh Reload &amp; mTLS Security</h3>
            <p>
              Hot reloads propagate across the cluster over encrypted TCP framing using <code>ClusterWireMsg::Reload</code>. The cluster mesh uses <strong>Rustls 0.23</strong> for mutual TLS (mTLS): both client and server authenticate using trusted root CAs (<code>ClusterTlsConfig</code>), completely isolating rogue nodes.
            </p>

