          <div class="parity-card card">
            <div class="parity-title-row">
              <h3>Stack Bytecode VM</h3>
              <span class="badge">Default Engine (<code>--vm</code>)</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Precompiles AST into compact bytecode chunks (<code>.shaec</code>). Evaluates instructions on a fast virtual operand stack with indexed local slots, upvalue capture, and direct jumps.
            </p>
            <ul class="parity-feature-list">
              <li><strong>Startup Latency:</strong> ~3 ms cold start</li>
              <li><strong>Loop Throughput:</strong> ~80,000+ ops/sec</li>
              <li><strong>AOT Ready:</strong> Direct bytecode serialization</li>
              <li><strong>JIT Integration:</strong> Seamless Cranelift tiering</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="parity-card card">
            <div class="parity-title-row">
              <h3>Tree-Walking AST Evaluator</h3>
              <span class="badge">Instant Scripting (<code>--ast</code>)</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Traverses the Abstract Syntax Tree directly without bytecode compilation passes. Ideal for rapid one-off scripting, macro transformations, and developer debugging.
            </p>
            <ul class="parity-feature-list">
              <li><strong>Compilation Delay:</strong> 0 ms (Zero compile phase)</li>
              <li><strong>Debug Introspection:</strong> Exact source AST spans</li>
              <li><strong>Memory Footprint:</strong> Low overhead for single runs</li>
              <li><strong>Engine Parity:</strong> 290+ tests pass identically</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
